# ===================================================================
#  Supporting_Information — .gitignore
#  Marine eutrophication footprint of reactive nitrogen (analysis code)
#
#  Philosophy: this repository tracks the ANALYSIS CODE plus a couple of
#  small input tables. The large raw data and the regenerable model
#  outputs are NOT tracked here. The full working folder is ~28 GB and
#  GitHub rejects any single file larger than 100 MB, so the bulk data
#  belongs on an external archive (e.g. Zenodo). See README.md ->
#  "Data availability" for exactly where each dataset comes from.
#
#  Every file currently >50 MB in this tree is a .h5, .csv, .yxdb or
#  .shp, so the rules below keep an accidental `git add .` well under
#  GitHub's limit.
# ===================================================================

# ------------- Large raw-data / array formats (get from source) -------------
*.h5
*.hdf
*.hdf5
*.nc
*.nc4
*.grd
*.grib
*.tif
*.tiff
# .yxdb = Alteryx databases (the large MRIO / GLORIA data in folder E)
*.yxdb
*.npy
*.npz
*.mat
*.parquet
*.feather
*.pkl
*.zip

# ------------- GIS shapefile bundles (third-party boundaries) -------------
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.sbn
*.sbx
*.qix
*.qpj

# ------------- CSV: ignored by default -------------
#  Most CSVs here are multi-GB CF matrices, gridded emissions, or per-cell
#  outputs. The small, essential INPUT tables are whitelisted just below.
*.csv
!**/Wang2025_leaching_factors.csv
!A_agricultural_leaching/MouthID_PCR2.csv
!0_shape_files/0_gridcells_LME_mapped.csv
!0_shape_files/5_LME_Country_match/LME_country_match.csv
!D_Final_Database/country_to_continent.csv
#  To ALSO publish a specific small result table, add a line such as:
#     !B_airborne_NH3/NH3_impact_by_country_sector.csv
#     !C_airborne_NOx/NOx_impact_by_country_sector.csv
#  (confirm the file is < 50 MB first).

# ------------- Regenerable model outputs -------------
A_agricultural_leaching/5. outputs_crops/
A_agricultural_leaching/6. outputs_grazing/
D_Final_Database/*.xlsx
D_Final_Database/5. outputs_crops/

# ------------- Case study: scripts tracked, generated results/figures kept local -------------
F_Practical_case/1. results/
F_Practical_case/1. results_anchored/
F_Practical_case/2. figures/
F_Practical_case/*.docx
F_Practical_case/*.xlsx
!F_Practical_case/SI_2_Supplementary Table.xlsx
F_Practical_case/.RData
F_Practical_case/.Rhistory
F_Practical_case/node_modules/
F_Practical_case/package.json
F_Practical_case/package-lock.json

# ------------- Regenerable result tables of the anchored batch -------------
E_MRIO_GLORIA_Satellites/PBA_before_after_*.xlsx
E_MRIO_GLORIA_Satellites/1b. GLORIAv60_Eutrophication_Satellites_anchored/
E_MRIO_GLORIA_Satellites/2. GLORIA_vs_EEZ_check/
_before_rerun_Nov2026/

# ------------- Archived / scratch / superseded -------------
**/0. Old/
**/0_Old/
**/Old/
Model input/

# ------------- Editor backups & caches -------------
*.bak
*.bak_*
*~
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.spyproject/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ------------- OS / OneDrive / Office junk -------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
*.tmp

# ------------- Local secrets — NEVER commit -------------
#  a_download_adalibieke.py ships with placeholders and reads TPDC_USER /
#  TPDC_PASS from the environment; if you store your personal credentials in
#  a local file instead, name it so one of these patterns catches it.
.env
*secret*
*credentials*
tpdc_login.*

# ------------- raw EDGAR v8.1 sector files (huge; re-download via the extraction scripts) -------------
**/[0-9]. EDGAR*/*
!**/[0-9]. EDGAR*/*.py
**/_to_delete/
